        // and its target is fixed; however the mutant difference depends on whether the external call
        // succeeds or fails. To force the external call to fail, we can make the fixed target (the
        // address hard-coded in C) be a contract that reverts by deploying a contract at that address.
        // We cannot deploy at an arbitrary address normally, so instead we simulate the adversarial
        // behaviour by making that hard-coded address be a contract that already exists in the test
        // environment: we deploy a forwarding contract at that hard-coded address using CREATE2.

